  "verses": {
    "verse": [
      [
        "Amazing grace, how sweet the sound",
        "that saved a wretch like me.",
        "I once was lost, but now am found,",
        "was blind, but now I see."
      ],
      [
        "'Twas grace that taught my heart to fear,",
        "and grace my fears relieved;",
        "how precious did that grace appear",
        "the hour I first believed!"
      ],
      [
        "Through many dangers, toils, and snares,",
        "I have already come;",
        "'tis grace has brought me safe thus far,",
        "and grace will lead me home."
      ],
      [
        "The Lord has promised good to me,",
        "His word my hope secures;",
        "He will my shield and portion be",
        "as long as life endures."
      ],
      [
        "Yes, when this flesh and heart shall fail,",
        "and mortal life shall cease,",
        "I shall possess, within the veil,",
        "a life of joy and peace."
      ],
      [
        "The earth shall soon dissolve like snow,",
        "the sun forbear to shine;",
        "but God, who call'd me here below,",
        "will be for ever mine."
      ]
    ]
  },
  "arrangerNotes": "3/4 time. Verified against the Wikipedia LilyPond score: slurred two-note syllables are written as separate notes. The 'I once was lost, but now am found' phrase has its own melody (5-3 / 5-3 on 'once was', 6-1 / 1-6 on 'now am'), not a repeat of the first line. Range low 5 to 5, minLayout 11 on both drums. C and D arrangements use identical degree sequences (both fit their drums). Lyrics of the added verses: Verses 2–6: John Newton's original text, Olney Hymns (1779), Book I, Hymn 41, as transcribed on Wikisource from the 1840 edition (https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Olney_Hymns_(1840)/Book_1/Hymn_41).",
  "verified": true
